<article class="env-corollary" id="0E3C11">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E3C11">Corollary <span data-tag="0E3C11">6.2.3.5</span>.</a> Let $\calX $ be a semitopos, and let $f: U \rightarrow X$ be a morphism in $\calX $. The following conditions are equivalent: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
If we regard $f$ as an object of the $\infty $-category $\calX _{/X}$, then $\tau _{\leq -1}(f)$ is a final object of $\calX _{/X}$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
The Čech nerve $\mCech (f)$ is a simplicial resolution of $X$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>